{"name":"Husky","hex":"#e0ebfa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Husky","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Eskimo person.","Alternative form of husky"]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Any of the languages of the Eskimo peoples."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Husky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Husky","blocks":[{"text":"Husky is a general term for a type of dog used in the polar regions, primarily and specifically for work as sled dogs. It also refers to a traditional northern type, notable for its cold-weather tolerance and overall hardiness. Modern racing huskies that maintain arctic breed traits represent an ever-changing crossbreed of the fastest dogs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Huskiesatrest.jpg/330px-Huskiesatrest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husky","wikidata":"Q3244349"},{"title":"Husky (rapper)","blocks":[{"text":"Dmitry Nikolayevich Kuznetsov, better known by his stage name Husky, is a Russian rapper from Ulan-Ude. His music is known for its use of somber and evocative lyricism, complex rhyming schemes, and musical techniques like assonance and alliteration. His provocative songs are known for being poetically contradictory to his gopnik image."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Rapper_Haski_on_Stereoleto_2020.jpg/330px-Rapper_Haski_on_Stereoleto_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husky_(rapper)","wikidata":"Q39382321"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg/500px-DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg/500px-DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai